  "about": "PRO-561 render-then-lint fixtures. Each probe replaces the placeholder sentence of a section in the unit-test draft, is rendered by T5 and then linted. source_hard says whether the Markdown pre-check alone (--source-only) already hard-fails with that rule; rule is the hard fail the rendered view must report (null: must pass). N2-alt-role lands in the PDF view because WeasyPrint lays out alt text when the image does not load; the HTML view reads it too (RenderThenLintTests.test_html_view_reads_reader_visible_attributes). The *-glued-* cases put hidden text directly against the next word; the stray-head cases put a <head> tag inside the body (RenderThenLintTests.test_stray_head_keeps_html_view covers a later section). The F1-* cases (PRO-618) hide glued text in ways the HTML view must parse like a browser (\"/>\" on a non-void element, the first duplicate attribute, CSS comments, <template>) or now detects directly (<style> class/id rules outside @media print, font-size:0, opacity:0, color:transparent, <noscript>); the F2-* cases pin the hidden-subtree boundaries, including a <br> inside the hidden span and adjacent hidden spans that join up. The F1-text-* cases (Grok QA B1 on PRO-633) are visible text that is contiguous in the delivered page, joined by a soft hyphen, a zero-width character or inline formatting that ends mid-word: they must pass.",
